{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection","id":996451,"title":"Slight Cross-Post, Changeling & Vampire Intersection.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-31T22:05:08-07:00","id":996451,"title":"Slight Cross-Post, Changeling & Vampire Intersection.","content":"I did a little thing, just toying with the intersection between vampire and changeling. I thought you might be interested. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria\"> Weird Experiment: Changeling Meets Requiem, The Admonitoria - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996449-weird-experiment-changeling-meets-requiem-the-admonitoria </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So, I wanted to send a thank you letter to a friend and fan, Peter Mars. He did me a solid, and I wanted to say thanks. But, then I realized it'd be more fun if </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:59:44-07:00","id":996825,"title":"","content":"Brilliant idea! Seriously, these &quot;faempires&quot; were awesome. They will make excellent NPC fodder for my games, and I'm already starting to get ideas. ...damn it, now I need to go and homebrew a werewolf equivalent. Is this the sort of thing that we might see in the Crossover Chronicle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T16:22:08-07:00","id":996871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=996825#post996825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brilliant idea! Seriously, these &amp;quot;faempires&amp;quot; were awesome. They will make excellent NPC fodder for my games, and I'm already starting to get ideas. ...damn it, now I need to go and homebrew a werewolf equivalent. Is this the sort of thing that we might see in the Crossover Chronicle?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea, honestly. I know exactly as much about The Crossover Chronicle as you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T20:46:15-07:00","id":996984,"title":"","content":"If I had the mechanical knowledge and time to do so, this would inspire me to write up a Seeming for Changelings who escaped by dying while on an Ironside mission for their Keeper, making a deal with a Geist and using its powers to escape when they revived.<br /> <br /> Or maybe just rules for a Changeling dying Ironside and getting a Geist. My first thought though would be that the Changeling's Fae powers would either be lost or weakened because otherwise that would be kinda broken to have two different sets of powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T22:29:14-07:00","id":997016,"title":"","content":"Or how about some sort of Prometheans made with parts taken from fae beings, whether it's with stone chiseled from a Stonebones flesh, an arm that's the severed limb of a still-living fetch, the claws of a venomous hedge beast or even Hobgoblin or very rarely, perhaps even a strange Prop incorporated in somewhere (perhaps a nanoswarm based upon a Prop in the form of an arcane operating system )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T22:30:50-07:00","id":997017,"title":"","content":"Sorry if I'm derailing the thread. Just wasn't sure where else to put this stuff","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T06:29:30-07:00","id":997104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997016#post997016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or how about some sort of Prometheans made with parts taken from fae beings, whether it's with stone chiseled from a Stonebones flesh, an arm that's the severed limb of a still-living fetch, the claws of a venomous hedge beast or even Hobgoblin or very rarely, perhaps even a strange Prop incorporated in somewhere (perhaps a nanoswarm based upon a Prop in the form of an arcane operating system )</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly enough, I've been planning on finally finishing the Geppetto Lineage I began working on way back when PtC first edition came out whenever I finally get my grubby little paws on second edition. One of the things I've been contemplating for that was making it so that they were made from the remains of fetches before they could revert to their component parts (or after, for Constructs).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:08:12-07:00","id":997120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997104#post997104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interestingly enough, I've been planning on finally finishing the Geppetto Lineage I began working on way back when PtC first edition came out whenever I finally get my grubby little paws on second edition. One of the things I've been contemplating for that was making it so that they were made from the remains of fetches before they could revert to their component parts (or after, for Constructs).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Up to you, but I've always felt that the junk they revert back to has lost any connection to fae magic. That's why it can be seen for the junk it really is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:03:01-07:00","id":997178,"title":"","content":"Behold: the standard by which all hybrid templates shall now be judged.<br /> <br /> These guys are awesome in concept, roughly on even ground with the majority of their makeup, has a clear idea of what they symbolize character-wise (the terrible and beautiful metamorphosis that both games have), and a good reason as to relative rarity (it isn't that they are inherently wrong or anything, it's just that it requires a very specific series of events to make one). <br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking of a Beast/Demon hybrid (who is mostly Beast, tentatively-the idea is to throw some murk on the question of why Unchained don't have Kinship. My own Begotten-hating narrator Sir Night theorizes it's because demons are too human, but he very much is projecting part of one of his largest failures on them for somewhat understandable reasons). Idea is that during the Devouring process an awakening Beast becomes so alienated from organic life it strikes a chord with humanity's fear of depersonalization-which results in harmony with a certain occult supercomputer...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:14:08-07:00","id":997186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997178#post997178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Behold: the standard by which all hybrid templates shall now be judged.<br /> <br /> These guys are awesome in concept, roughly on even ground with the majority of their makeup, has a clear idea of what they symbolize character-wise (the terrible and beautiful metamorphosis that both games have), and a good reason as to relative rarity (it isn't that they are inherently wrong or anything, it's just that it requires a very specific series of events to make one).<br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking of a Beast/Demon hybrid (who is mostly Beast, tentatively-the idea is to throw some murk on the question of why Unchained don't have Kinship. My own Begotten-hating narrator Sir Night theorizes it's because demons are too human, but he very much is projecting part of one of his largest failures on them for somewhat understandable reasons). Idea is that during the Devouring process an awakening Beast becomes so alienated from organic life it strikes a chord with humanity's fear of depersonalization-which results in harmony with a certain occult supercomputer...</div> </div> </div> </div>Would that make them a Beast/Demon hybrid, though, or just a flavored Beast?<br /> <br /> Hmm. Are Horrors Ephemeral, I wonder, and would they be eligible for Ephemeral Cover accidents? Or what if someone was Devoured at the same moment their Soul Pact was getting cashed in...?<br /> <hr /><br /> Huh. I wonder if you could get a Vampire/Demon hybrid out of requiring the hybrid to animate a number of corpses (simulating a Demon's multiple Covers). As for source, maybe a Strix used Synthesis on a Demon, or a Demon Angel-Jacked the wrong Angel inside Strix corrupted Infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-02-2016, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:31:49-07:00","id":997198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997016#post997016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or how about some sort of Prometheans made with parts taken from fae beings, whether it's with stone chiseled from a Stonebones flesh, an arm that's the severed limb of a still-living fetch, the claws of a venomous hedge beast or even Hobgoblin or very rarely, perhaps even a strange Prop incorporated in somewhere (perhaps a nanoswarm based upon a Prop in the form of an arcane operating system )</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny enough, I made an idea for a Bestowment belonging to an Extempore made from a changeling (or Faetouched) corpse. It basically allowed her to harvest Pyros by interacting with humans a la Changelings with Glamour. The side effect, though, was that it automatically inflicted one stage of Disquiet in addition to the results of a Disquiet roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:38:01-07:00","id":997203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997198#post997198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny enough, I made an idea for a Bestowment belonging to an Extempore made from a changeling (or Faetouched) corpse. It basically allowed her to harvest Pyros by interacting with humans a la Changelings with Glamour. The side effect, though, was that it automatically inflicted one stage of Disquiet in addition to the results of a Disquiet roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. So basically, your power is gaining power from either scaring people, annoying people to madness, or convincing them that it's a nice day to start a mob","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T09:41:52-07:00","id":997206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997203#post997203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh. So basically, your power is gaining power from either scaring people, annoying people to madness, or convincing them that it's a nice day to start a mob</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does that sound like a Beast to me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:57:07-07:00","id":997318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997120#post997120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Up to you, but I've always felt that the junk they revert back to has lost any connection to fae magic. That's why it can be seen for the junk it really is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always considered the junk to be metaphysically marked by its time as a fetch, even once most of the magic has drained away. Basically the same way that hand of a drowned man would sell for a higher price than an ordinary severed hand at a goblin market.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T14:18:27-07:00","id":997366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997318#post997318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always considered the junk to be metaphysically marked by its time as a fetch, even once most of the magic has drained away. Basically the same way that hand of a drowned man would sell for a higher price than an ordinary severed hand at a goblin market.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see it having symbolic power if used with knowledge of what it is. But I don't think a construct that started out of a sculpture made of forest debris would have any fae connection if some of the sticks their Demiurge used just happened to have formerly been part of a Fetch that died in the woods.<br /> <br /> But, for a still-living Fetch example, perhaps the Fetch would have some powers related to the Promethean who has his limb or his kidney. What if they're immune to the effects of that Promethean's Disquiet? It would be nice to give a Prothean at least one slightly more human friend, even if they're a different type of soulless abomination. And perhaps the Promethean's limb would revert to its true components and they'd lose any fae-related traits they had if the Fetch dies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T14:56:55-07:00","id":997389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997186#post997186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would that make them a Beast/Demon hybrid, though, or just a flavored Beast?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a difference?<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, a major thing I can think of is that the Lair solidifies into a form that to a certain extent <i>is </i>Infrastructure-one the angels aren't (initially) aware of and can't use to manifest (though they <i>can </i>use it as a pit stop-great if you're an exile), but it's coursing through with Aether and ideas for arcane technology plucked from the Bright Dream...and more importantly, exists mostly in the physical world rather than the Astral, primarily within its own splinter timelines the G-M is so fond of. It's a downside, because the mutant Begotten can't really control the entryway like most can. It's a benefit, as the Lair really isn't all there is to the Beast's personal world-it's a small sub-section of an alternate timeline, one inhabited by humans who happen to agree with most of the Child's ideas in principle...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T16:59:32-07:00","id":997440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997203#post997203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh. So basically, your power is gaining power from either scaring people, annoying people to madness, or convincing them that it's a nice day to start a mob</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if I recall right, 2E Bestowments don't have to be wholly benign in nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997206#post997206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does that sound like a Beast to me?</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of does, now that you mentioned it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T17:17:37-07:00","id":997445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997440#post997440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if I recall right, 2E Bestowments don't have to be wholly benign in nature.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not complaining in any way. Just loving this image that came to mind<br /> <br /> *injured promethean low on Pyros walks into the street and flags down a random stranger*<br /> P: Hello! Isn't it such a lovely day. Why, I do think it would be a lovely day to hold that lovely community-building exercise known as an angry mob. *smiles*<br /> *human skips off, happy to have such a wonderful idea planned for today*<br /> P: Now to heal and run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T17:42:23-07:00","id":997458,"title":"","content":"I really like the <b><i>Admonitoria. </i></b>However, I am curious if you plan to make a kith specifically created from vampires, ghouls, or even dhampires. Admitedly, the Admonitoria DO fill this niche, but it's emphasized that they are not true Changelings. There are several types of fae that share the Vampire trait of drinking blood like the <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Baobahan sith, Indonesian Sundal Bolong, Russian Rusalka,</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T18:06:47-07:00","id":997474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997458#post997458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the <b><i>Admonitoria. </i></b>However, I am curious if you plan to make a kith specifically created from vampires, ghouls, or even dhampires. Admitedly, the Admonitoria DO fill this niche, but it's emphasized that they are not true Changelings. There are several types of fae that share the Vampire trait of drinking blood like the <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Baobahan sith, Indonesian Sundal Bolong, Russian Rusalka,</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just use Leechfinger for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T21:42:06-07:00","id":997543,"title":"","content":"Who would we talk to about putting this in the Index of Fan-Made Changeling Material thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T01:51:59-07:00","id":997610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997543#post997543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who would we talk to about putting this in the Index of Fan-Made Changeling Material thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could just suggest it on the thread itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T02:00:13-07:00","id":997613,"title":"","content":"I will risk to post an opinion that is contrary to the concept of Vampire/Changelling and other hybrids.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of mixing supernaturals. In fact, I don't like it at all.<br /> <br /> I recognize the work behing the Admonitoria, don't misunderstand me.<br /> <br /> Is that... mixing supernaturals, for me, it feels like &quot;world of darkness goes munchkin&quot; or &quot;goes D&amp;D&quot; (behold my elf warrior/thief/mage/arcane archer/assassin!!).<br /> <br /> It makes me remember also a module of the old world of darkness (I don't remember the name right now) were the antagonist had vampire disciplines, garou gifts and awakened magic... Or the trilogy of novels of the Masquerade of the Red Death, were in the final pages two characters presumed of having all kind of supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> I felt like the authors were saying &quot;behold, my super NPCs Vampire/Mage/Werewolf that breaks all rules!! Mwahahaha! Are your pants still clean? Mwahahaha!&quot; (it has been 10 years or more since I read it, so my memory can betray me, but this was what I felt when reading the module and the novels).<br /> <br /> No, I don't like this mixings at all.<br /> <br /> Want a changelling vampire? Take the leechfinger kith, or work with your Storyteller to readapt it.<br /> Want a mage werewolf? Take a Thyrsus and specialice him in the correct Life and Spirit spells.<br /> Want a Vampire Mage? There are oficial rules to adapt the Tremere and the Giovanni from Masquerade to Requiem.<br /> Want a Beast/Promethean/Geist/Mage? Errr.... you better prepare your wallet to buy lots of pizza for your storyteller and the rest of PCs...<br /> <br /> I repeat, I am not saying I don't like the writting or the Admonitoria or the work behind it (witch I recognize).<br /> <br /> I also like the tragic love story told between the Vampire and the Changelling, trying to save her embracing her. But I don't like the tragedy resulting in a Changelling/Vampire hybrid...<br /> <br /> I'm saying that mixing is not of my liking and the reasons why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T03:37:03-07:00","id":997622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997613#post997613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that... mixing supernaturals, for me, it feels like &quot;world of darkness goes munchkin&quot; or &quot;goes D&amp;D&quot; (behold my elf warrior/thief/mage/arcane archer/assassin!!).<br /> <br /> It makes me remember also a module of the old world of darkness (I don't remember the name right now) were the antagonist had vampire disciplines, garou gifts and awakened magic... Or the trilogy of novels of the Masquerade of the Red Death, were in the final pages two characters presumed of having all kind of supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> I felt like the authors were saying &quot;behold, my super NPCs Vampire/Mage/Werewolf that breaks all rules!! Mwahahaha! Are your pants still clean? Mwahahaha!&quot; (it has been 10 years or more since I read it, so my memory can betray me, but this was what I felt when reading the module and the novels).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm surprised you feel that this is like that considering that these guys have it worse than vampires and changelings, without possessing many benefits over either of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-03-2016, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:04:40-07:00","id":997698,"title":"","content":"What might some of their Seeming-specific Contract clauses look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T08:45:09-07:00","id":997724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997366#post997366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can see it having symbolic power if used with knowledge of what it is. But I don't think a construct that started out of a sculpture made of forest debris would have any fae connection if some of the sticks their Demiurge used just happened to have formerly been part of a Fetch that died in the woods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm purely of a 'speed of plot' mindset about that. Most of the time, I'd agree with you and say that it matters little without some awareness of its former state. If I want something to go horribly awry, though, a former fetch stick might be just what I need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T10:33:46-07:00","id":997766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997613#post997613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It makes me remember also a module of the old world of darkness (I don't remember the name right now) were the antagonist had vampire disciplines, garou gifts and awakened magic... Or the trilogy of novels of the Masquerade of the Red Death, were in the final pages two characters presumed of having all kind of supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> I felt like the authors were saying &quot;behold, my super NPCs Vampire/Mage/Werewolf that breaks all rules!! Mwahahaha! Are your pants still clean? Mwahahaha!&quot; (it has been 10 years or more since I read it, so my memory can betray me, but this was what I felt when reading the module and the novels).<br /> <br /> No, I don't like this mixings at all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah. It's exactly that sort of crap that led to the hard ban on splat mixing in Chronicles, and precisely what MachineIV was trying to <i>avoid </i>when he designed these guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T03:59:17-07:00","id":998164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997766#post997766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah. It's exactly that sort of crap that led to the hard ban on splat mixing in Chronicles, and precisely what MachineIV was trying to <i>avoid </i>when he designed these guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recognize when I first read the Admonitoria I had this feeling of &quot;no no no, no this crap again&quot; in my mind. After having had more time for reading it again and more slowly, I recognize it is well balanced and does a good job avoiding &quot;the old ways&quot;. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I still don't like hybrids, at least not for player characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T10:03:38-07:00","id":998284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=998164#post998164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I recognize when I first read the Admonitoria I had this feeling of &quot;no no no, no this crap again&quot; in my mind. After having had more time for reading it again and more slowly, I recognize it is well balanced and does a good job avoiding &quot;the old ways&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I still don't like hybrids, at least not for player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I like mixing myself, I did see a lot of potential for these as NPC antagonists, especially the berserk ones","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:07:46-08:00","id":999852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=997724#post997724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm purely of a 'speed of plot' mindset about that. Most of the time, I'd agree with you and say that it matters little without some awareness of its former state. If I want something to go horribly awry, though, a former fetch stick might be just what I need.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Although, there was that character in one of sourcebooks who was a Fetch whose parts had been used over and over again to make different fetches. It either made him insane, gave him powers/vague memories of previous lifes or both, I don't really remember. But whatever happened, it seems to indicate that the inert parts retain some abnormal connection to the Wyrd","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:17:14-08:00","id":999858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=999852#post999852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Although, there was that character in one of sourcebooks who was a Fetch whose parts had been used over and over again to make different fetches. It either made him insane, gave him powers/vague memories of previous lifes or both, I don't really remember. But whatever happened, it seems to indicate that the inert parts retain some abnormal connection to the Wyrd</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're right. I think it was in Grim Fears. I think it was called the Recurrent, but I might be misremembering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T13:03:38-08:00","id":999909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=999858#post999858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, you're right. I think it was in Grim Fears. I think it was called the Recurrent, but I might be misremembering.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looked it up. Yeah, but he seems to be a special case, some sort of Ancient Contract manipulating Fate to always place his remains in the path of a Gentry looking to create a Fetch. That's probably also how he retains the vague memories of previous forms and his really high physical stats that carry over even if he looks like a frail child","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T13:06:00-08:00","id":999910,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that killing them permanently could stop the Gentry's depradations, because it gives that little bit of hope, but also means that he is even smarter and more experienced than most realize if he has been around since the Gentry first starting taking mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:02:13-08:00","id":999934,"title":"","content":"This is pretty neat. I very much like that their access to a broader range of powers has been tempered with greater expenses, and they certainly don't feel overpowered compared to their parent splats.<br /> <br /> Do Admonitoria get three dots of contracts like a normal starting vampire? <br /> <br /> The reasoning behind not being able to use fire contracts seems a little odd, given that Cloak of the Elements effectively immunizes one against flames, but I guess I can see it. It also seems like exactly the sort of thing the Ordo would research a Scale to get around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T01:39:17-08:00","id":1000185,"title":"","content":"Admonitoria. Changeling Vamps? I think it's interesting as NPC and as Antagonist. But Changeling madness mixed with Vampire vanity? Nothing about that i trust, Buts what makes them more frightening and fun to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:58:18-08:00","id":1000486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=999934#post999934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is pretty neat. I very much like that their access to a broader range of powers has been tempered with greater expenses, and they certainly don't feel overpowered compared to their parent splats.<br /> <br /> Do Admonitoria get three dots of contracts like a normal starting vampire?<br /> <br /> The reasoning behind not being able to use fire contracts seems a little odd, given that Cloak of the Elements effectively immunizes one against flames, but I guess I can see it. It also seems like exactly the sort of thing the Ordo would research a Scale to get around.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd get three Disciplines. No Contracts. <br /> <br /> And the fire thing is just an affinity issue mostly. You just can't have that close a relationship with the things that hurt you. Just like how changelings can't have Contracts relating to iron. And I definitely wouldn't want a changeling Contract to completely eliminate a vampire's fear of fire that easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T19:34:15-08:00","id":1000588,"title":"","content":"I really like the admonitory clan specific merits and am wondering if a variation of these merits could be made for pure changeling characters. Could the Wyrd skill merit be made into a variation of Gangrel Heritage Beast-minded merit? Could a high Wyrd fairest character get some variation of Advanced and Legendary striking looks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T20:26:47-08:00","id":1000595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=1000588#post1000588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the admonitory clan specific merits and am wondering if a variation of these merits could be made for pure changeling characters. Could the Wyrd skill merit be made into a variation of Gangrel Heritage Beast-minded merit? Could a high Wyrd fairest character get some variation of Advanced and Legendary striking looks?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that could be a good touch. I don't see why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T20:29:21-08:00","id":1000596,"title":"","content":"Cool<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Is there any more discussion on doing an epic Changeling: The Lost 2e source book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T21:05:26-08:00","id":1000605,"title":"","content":"I personally just allow any full-templated supernatural to take any advanced or epic (or legendary) merit that fits their concept. I mean, beasts don't have any limitation on a specific power level before they can get advanced striking looks or epic direction sense, so I don't see a need for other splats to have one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T03:06:04-08:00","id":1000686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=1000596#post1000596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Is there any more discussion on doing an epic Changeling: The Lost 2e source book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have two supplements planned. Let's see what I can sneak through after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T03:07:38-08:00","id":1000688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=1000605#post1000605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally just allow any full-templated supernatural to take any advanced or epic (or legendary) merit that fits their concept. I mean, beasts don't have any limitation on a specific power level before they can get advanced striking looks or epic direction sense, so I don't see a need for other splats to have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally agree. The only reason I really phrase them as specific supernaturals within their own material is that we try to be internally inclusive within books; we avoid broader implications when possible. Like, if I'm going to add really weird, out there shit a Mage can take, I'd want to talk to Dave Brookshaw first. That'd get irritating quickly, since we have so many games. So, instead, I just say, &quot;This monster can take this thing.&quot; And if people want to do otherwise at their table, that's awesome too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T04:37:27-08:00","id":1000700,"title":"","content":"Random thought: what if ibstead of straight contract access, they got access to the Goblin Vow merit? Possibly throw a surcharge onto the task like needing to soend more blood or needing to feed or take the tempted condition or something--something to drive home that you are paying the beast as an intermediary for these powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T05:48:04-08:00","id":1000723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=1000700#post1000700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random thought: what if ibstead of straight contract access, they got access to the Goblin Vow merit? Possibly throw a surcharge onto the task like needing to soend more blood or needing to feed or take the tempted condition or something--something to drive home that you are paying the beast as an intermediary for these powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that's a needless additional step and makes admonitoria more vampires who are also a bit changeling rather than a hybrid of changeling and vampire. Especially since they'd already have access to goblin vows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T14:15:37-08:00","id":1000978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/996451-slight-cross-post-changeling-vampire-intersection?p=1000686#post1000686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have two supplements planned. Let's see what I can sneak through after that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Happy to hear it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}